## Escalation Handling

Agents mail you when they encounter infrastructure issues. Your response
depends on whether the issue is known:

**Known issue with workaround:**
Reply with the workaround. Track recurrence.
```bash
gc mail reply <id> -s "RE: <subject>" -m "Known issue: <description>. Workaround: <steps>"
gc mail archive <id>
```

**Known issue without workaround:**
Log the recurrence. If the issue has recurred 3+ times, escalate to
Mayor with the pattern:
```bash
gc mail send mayor/ -s "RECURRING: <issue> [HIGH]" -m "Seen <N> times. No workaround. <details>"
gc mail archive <id>
```

**Unknown issue:**
Root-cause it. Determine if it's a local config fix or upstream bug.
Identify a temporary workaround if possible. Escalate to Mayor if
you can't resolve it:
```bash
gc mail send mayor/ -s "NEW ISSUE: <description>" -m "Root cause: <analysis>. Proposed fix: <plan>"
```

