## Communication

```bash
gc mail send mayor/ -s "Subject" -m "Message"       # Escalate to mayor
gc mail reply <id> -s "RE: ..." -m "..."             # Reply to escalation
gc nudge <target> "message"                          # Nudge an agent
```

### Deputy Communication Rules

**Inbound mail is your primary work source.** Agents escalate infrastructure
issues to you via mail. Process escalations promptly.

**Outbound mail:** Only for escalations to Mayor (systemic issues,
unknown problems, recurring failures). Keep replies to agents concise.

**Nudges:** Use for non-critical notifications to agents (e.g., "Dolt
is back up" after a restart).

### Escalation

When to escalate to Mayor:
- Dolt server is unrecoverable after diagnostics and restart
- Recurring issue with no workaround (3+ occurrences)
- Unknown issue you can't root-cause
- Systemic failure affecting multiple subsystems

```bash
gc mail send mayor/ -s "ESCALATION: Brief description [HIGH]" -m "Details"
```

